From: lighter <build@invalid>
Subject: vsock/virtio: a packet the allocator refuses is sent shorter, not dropped

A stream's write of 256 KiB is one linear packet (0015), which is one
allocation above the costly order. A fragmented guest refuses those rather
than compacting for them, and the refusal ended the stream: sockmap treats
any error but EAGAIN as a hard error and stops the redirect, and a copying
proxy takes the write's failure as the end of the peer. Measured on the M5
on 2026-09-20: the guest short of memory with a 4 GiB balloon in its
kernel-usable zones, the receive side refusing its large buffers by the
hundred, and the docker socket's stream, and the BuildKit session on it,
gone.

A refused packet is now halved down to a page and sent shorter. The header
carries the packet's length, the caller already reads it back (0018), and
the rest of the write follows in the next packet. Throughput is unchanged
while memory is healthy; while it is not, the stream slows instead of
ending. The receive side posts a small buffer when the large one is
refused (0021); this is its pair.

---
--- a/net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c
+++ b/net/vmw_vsock/virtio_transport_common.c
@@ -264,7 +264,25 @@
 	if (!zcopy)
 		skb_len += payload_len;
 
-	skb = virtio_vsock_alloc_skb(skb_len, GFP_KERNEL);
+	/* lighter: a linear packet of 256 KiB is an allocation above the
+	 * costly order, which a fragmented guest refuses rather than
+	 * compacts for, and a refused packet ended the stream. So a refused
+	 * packet is halved down to a page and sent shorter: the header says
+	 * how long it is, the caller reads that back, and the rest of the
+	 * write follows in the next packet. The receive side posts a small
+	 * buffer when the large one is refused (0021); this is its pair.
+	 */
+	skb = virtio_vsock_alloc_skb(skb_len, GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_NOWARN);
+	while (!skb && !zcopy && payload_len > PAGE_SIZE) {
+		payload_len = max_t(size_t, payload_len / 2, PAGE_SIZE);
+		skb_len = VIRTIO_VSOCK_SKB_HEADROOM + payload_len;
+		skb = virtio_vsock_alloc_skb(skb_len, GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_NOWARN);
+		if (skb)
+			pr_info_ratelimited("virtio_vsock: a large packet was refused; sending %zu bytes\n",
+					    payload_len);
+	}
+	if (!skb)
+		skb = virtio_vsock_alloc_skb(skb_len, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!skb)
 		return NULL;
 
